  "selection_rule": "Runtime reference: only the Lua base and type system, channel, contract, process, registry, time, JSON, HTTP client, security, UUID, filesystem, SQL and TTY pages used by Bee app authors; the SQL reference includes sql.builder. Runtime tutorials, internals, general guides and platform material are excluded. Bee contracts: the docs pages that state an implemented callable boundary or the path a frozen artifact travels (application, threads, placement, gateway, carrier, storage, ui, harness, approvals, registry, platform). Component: one page per Bee component, written from the entries under src/<component>. Reference applications: one page per application source plus an index. Terminal toolkit: one page covering the tty module, bee.ui frame, viz, diagram and forms, and the bee.app client, checked against src/ui, src/app and tests/lua/ui. Reference drivers: generated by tools/corpus.py from src/driver. The corpus is digest-checked with make lint.",
